! Elyncia Factions ~ roster index

''The faction shelf.'' Each faction earns its own meme beside this index as its canon deepens;
the index holds the one-line roster and the summit standing. First enactment: ''the House of
Masks summit'' (YOLD 5492, Bureaucracy) — the Patroness's broadcast, two months prior, offering
any Factional representative a week's paid holiday to hear the Adventurer's Guild's contract
offer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/summit-roster>>

!! The Summit Roster

''Standing at the heart of it:'' the Order of Amaranth (hosts) · the Adventurer's Guild (the
contracting company) · the Amorphous Dreams Cabal · and the four the company walks in under —
the Spider-Mother's Priesthoods · the Gorgonne Diaspora Cabals · the Shattered Isles
Kaiju-Hunter Cabals · the Underworld Dojos. //(The Spider-Mother names one mask of a single
Arcana-Persona, alongside Grandmother Spider and Aracne-Jorogumo —
[[grandmother-spider|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/concepts/grandmother-spider]].)//

''Representatives at the tables:''

| Faction | The rep · the seed |
|---|---|
| Floating Librarians of Mu | a junior archivist chaperoning a flickering Voss-interface · locked records in a burned satellite stack |
| Brimstone Court forge-clans | a troll forge-envoy with a Named sidearm · clean-steel convoy escorts into the passes |
| Ironspine clans | a quarantine-rite matriarch smelling of spore-lamp smoke · a bloom outbreak needs putting down |
| Verdant Coil grove-factors | a factor whose contracts smell of resin · warding-cedar plantation rights |
| League naval guilds | a Third-Oar navigator in bronze-sun scales · route-prism charters for the reopened Hebros window |
| The Ouroborous Court | a knight-errant whose camp travels as their nation · joint action against the undead legions |
| Myrmidon cabals | a band-captain, old bronze and new paperwork · war-escort contracts in the northern passes |
| Khemet observers | one silent measurer with a reed pen · no stated mission; they came to watch |
| Asgard oath-brokers | a broker who signs nothing she cannot toast · god-witnessed patronage terms |
| The Lamplighters' Union | a soot-cloaked herm-tender with a lantern that has never rusted · the Neo-Thracian shrine-roads want relighting — [[full meme|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/factions/lamplighters-union]] |
| Bureau of Chronometry (Remnant) | a horologist wearing three disagreeing watches · the time-glitch stands as their oldest cold case |
| Cartographers of Unmade Places | the map-vendor's apprentice, paying in coin or true memory · they buy surveys of places that do not exist yet |
| The Crystal Court Troupe | tonight's entertainment — glass-sphere jugglers · the faction hiding on the stage |

''The empty seat.'' The Technomagic Tribes of Neo-Thracia sent no one — ''no one exits that
Nexus'': the storms and weather of the astral sea prevent departure for any lacking competent
navigators. Their seat stands set and empty at the summit, which every rep in the room reads
correctly as the evening's real agenda wearing a napkin.

''The rumor.'' The staff have twice tonight counted one more guest than the reservations hold.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/court-colors>>

!! Court Color Regimes

Derived from the court-dragon alignment canon, never invented whole:

* ''Seelie'' — gold + summer green
* ''Unseelie'' — black + winter violet
* ''Ouroborous'' — blue + bronze serpent-scale
* ''Brimstone'' — sulfur-yellow + ember red + ash grey

